  "2026-07-06T18:57:11.617Z",codex-cli-agent,"Evidence: imported 40 Semgrep Code findings from Semgrep_Code_Combined_Findings_2026_07_06.csv as child Issue items. Duplicate check before import found no existing Semgrep tracker items or Semgrep finding IDs in .agents/pm. Verification after import: pm search semgrep --status all --limit 60 returns 41 items (parent + 40 children); pm list --status all --parent pm-oz8u --limit 60 returns 40 child issues."
  "2026-07-06T19:36:47.451Z",codex-cli-agent,"Evidence update: imported the downloaded Semgrep 2026-07-06 CSV as one parent task plus 40 child Issue items, after all-status duplicate checks found no existing Semgrep lineage. Redacted the local absolute download path from the imported pm history/item metadata with pm history-redact; rg no longer finds the original local CSV path in tracked pm data. Verification: pm search semgrep --status all --limit 60 returns 41 items and pm list --status all --parent pm-oz8u --limit 60 returns 40 child issues; security:scan reports no credential-like secrets."
  "2026-07-24T12:17:13.096Z",claude-code-agent,"Whole-system audit evidence: active-only dedupe-audit found six fuzzy title clusters (29 candidate items, 23 merge suggestions), all within this imported Semgrep batch. Exact-title and parent-scope modes found zero. Manual comparison of pm-dtn1 and pm-y49x confirms distinct Semgrep finding IDs and distinct RegExp argument flows despite the same file/line signature; treat the fuzzy clusters as triage groups, not proven duplicates, and preserve external finding identity until each full record is reconciled against current Semgrep state."
  "2026-07-25T02:02:13.608Z","harness:codex","Evidence: completed the coordinated high-severity Semgrep remediation family. Generated Claude/Codex MCP wrappers select npx.cmd on Windows and spawn argv with shell disabled; the unused release shell option was removed. Full security scan, generator fixtures, wrapper execution tests, and 100% coverage pass."
  "2026-08-14T10:18:31.590Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-scan disposition 2026-08-14: the active fuzzy sweep still returns the same six clusters and 23 merge suggestions, all within this imported Semgrep batch. Full item bodies and compact histories confirm identical file-line signatures but distinct external finding IDs. The prior 2026-07-24 manual flow comparison remains the decisive evidence: these are triage groups, not proven duplicates. Preserve each external identity until a fresh Semgrep reconciliation proves the underlying flows or platform records have converged; no duplicate closures were performed."
  "2026-10-12T21:41:31.182Z","harness:codex","Fresh Chrome read2026-10-12: Semgrep findings route redirects to sign-in and displays acceptance of its terms. Current remote finding disposition cannot be verified in this authenticated session. GitHub Dependabot/code-scanning/secret-scanning inventories have0 open alerts and local pnpm audit reports no known vulnerabilities; those independent checks do not prove the external Semgrep inventory clear. Preserve the distinct imported finding identities and this owner open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-13T04:53:36.168Z","harness:codex","October13 live Chrome inspection: Semgrep findings URL redirects to login, and sign-in explicitly accepts terms of service. No findings triage or platform cleanliness is certified without access/terms approval. GitHub Dependabot code-scanning and secret-scanning inventories are empty. This canonical external triage stays open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-13T05:18:52.163Z","harness:codex","User approved Semgrep Terms acceptance on October13; authenticated Chrome project filter now shows51 open pm-cli findings, so the prior access limitation is resolved and the previous four-finding recall is not current evidence. Begin source/policy-backed static triage of exact finding identities, keeping unknown actor or rendering facts as unresolved and preserving input records."
  "2026-10-13T05:48:39.037Z","harness:codex","October13 authenticated Semgrep source review: 51 exact identities at scan revision 5fb0782f8b55064454a6b6efa04533fe6226e81b, preserving each record. Chrome successfully saved 44 false-positive dispositions and the filtered project now shows 7 open findings. Counterevidence: tracker prose is descriptive metadata, Git SHA-1 reproduces legacy object IDs, literal patterns are escaped or repository constants, history regexes are explicit authorized operator arguments, property reads do not mutate prototypes, writes reject reserved paths or use null prototypes, release observations are allowlisted, and MCP HTML encoding is confined to text contexts. Ignored IDs: 970869812, 970869811, 946720471, 946720470, 946720469, 992955295, 992955294, 893258048, 893258038, 1010864525, 963785848, 981403662, 970869813, 963785856, 963785854, 963785853, 963785852, 963785851, 963785850, 954817578, 893258077, 893258076, 893258073, 893258071, 893258069, 893258067, 893258065, 893258063, 1010864527, 1010864526, 963785849, 954817577, 954817576, 946720473, 946720472, 937509388, 928023199, 917550173, 981403661, 899808577, 946720468, 946720467, 946720466, 946720465. Further-review IDs: 963785855, 937509394, 937509393, 937509392, 937509391, 937509390, 937509389; bounded matching enhancement is tracked as child pm-0vqbl5. No scanner rule disabled and no security vulnerability confirmed by this static phase. Per-identity triage-finding/v0 artifact digest 829fcb1dff4a9e871ebe10c64f0a09aec9d19d30abcb328616443bf323d2df1b retained privately through the security plugin. Current findings link format is https://semgrep.dev/orgs/unbrained/findings/<ID>. The old July40 imported identities remain distinct historical records, not automatically closed from the new source inventory."
  "2026-10-13T06:06:21.930Z","harness:codex",Static triage is recorded and this parent is released to open while implementation/validation proceeds on its claimed bounded-matching child. The managed Semgrep project exposes a free rule-based rescan for main; use it after reviewed delivery to reconcile retained sink findings rather than disabling rules or prematurely labeling them fixed.
  "2026-10-13T06:13:46.685Z","harness:codex","Semgrep scan freshness is scoped correctly: October13 recent scans are PR diffs with0 findings, while the latest complete main scan is October9 and took23m58s with51 code findings and0 secrets/supply-chain findings. A fresh full main scan is necessary after the matcher delivery; a clean PR diff alone does not settle the retained baseline records."
  "2026-10-13T08:21:55.905Z","harness:codex","Completed exact historical reconciliation:32 distinct original July identities were read directly in authenticated Chrome and all report FIXED. Their activity datetime values are31 completions at2026-07-17T13:59:21.232Z and one at2026-08-07T14:03:45.981Z. Full live metadata and158 history entries were verified before mutation; each item was individually claimed, closed with structured evidence and the observed completed_at, released, and replay-verified. Original CSV bodies and identity links are preserved, and changelog-exclude prevents historical reconciliation from becoming new release notes. Private receipt digest c27334c3e4f3712f25bc15a6e745d2b5f458d61f03e9b14e3d0c2d0e8a097211. The7 distinct October matcher findings still require the planned full main rescan after delivery; pause this parent while candidate validation and review proceed."
  "2026-10-13T16:19:13.403Z","harness:codex","Begin full managed main rescan after reviewed source delivery: PR1455 merged at2026-10-13T16:17:46Z as f01d624d63b8971d7180758bbaf92880c8b6603d. Exact PR head a9cc7a11f passed all required checks,10394 tests with exact100% coverage, and the CodeRabbit full98-file review reports no actionable findings. Preserve the44 ignored false-positive identities and reconcile the7 old matcher records against this fresh full scan. Record operational closure in a reviewed main-based follow-up."
  "2026-10-13T16:50:03.462Z","harness:codex","The rule-based main scan was submitted and the project visibly confirms main Full Pending at October13 18:26 local display. The initial menu action required a delayed HTML branch-confirmation modal; only the confirmed Scan submission starts the scan. Release this parent while validating the independent telemetry tail-delivery finding, then reclaim for result reconciliation."
  "2026-10-13T17:16:26.308Z","harness:codex","Authenticated full main scan245435268 completed on October13 in21m42s with45 raw code observations,0 secrets,0 supply-chain findings and0 blocking findings. The project-and-main-filtered Open view has no matching findings. All7 retained matcher identities963785855,937509394,937509393,937509392,937509391,937509390,937509389 individually report FIXED at2026-10-13T16:50:05.365Z. Raw finding counts retain non-open historical/monitor observations; no rule was disabled. The45th observation is the local smoke harness assigning only fixed stdout/stderr diagnostic keys onto its own Error object, with no web response or user-controlled property names. Private fixed-identity receipt digest23c6e90da0634ce4b3175b68e5e6dbedf63d0ce75aa79297fb6604892c327e54 and scoped-zero-open screenshot digest78625c3d828e08bd57a2291b97cc6fdda0e82ea732c756cfa6ee3a859dcbc37d preserve the exact evidence."
